{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Elena. I'll start. From my perspective as team lead, I'm seeing a real tension on both sides. On one hand, several team members have been asking for longer uninterrupted work periods -- the constant context-switching between recurring meetings is clearly affecting deep work and, frankly, morale. On the other hand, I know there are legitimate concerns about reducing live touchpoints, especially around handoffs between teams. If we pick a day with no recurring internal meetings, we need to make sure the handoff expectations are clear and that people don't feel like coordination has become less respectful or less reliable. I think Wednesday is worth considering as the protected day, but I want to hear from the employee representative before I weigh in more specifically on which day and what guardrails we'd need."}
